  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Build a Persona & Problem Statement\r\n\r\n##Choose one scenario to focus on.\r\n\r\n**1. Identify The User**\r\n   - Give your user a name and basic context.\r\n   - Who are they in the situation? Why is the situation challenging for them?\r\n\r\n**2. Step Into Their Perspective**\r\n   - Complete the \"Says / Thinks / Feels / Does\" chart.\r\n   - Use evidence from the image and scenario to infer what this person might be experiencing.\r\n\r\n**3. Clarify The Core Need**\r\n   - Identify one specific frustration and one meaningful goal.\r\n   - Focus on what matters most to this user, not a solution.\r\n\r\n**4. Write A Clear Problem Statement**\r\n   - Use the template **\"[User] needs a way to [need] because [insight/reason].\"**\r\n   - Make sure your statement:\r\n      - Focuses on a need, not an app or feature.\r\n      - Is specific\r\n      - Is centered on the user\r\n\r\n**Tip:** When you are finished, you can use the AI Design Partner to review or strengthen your problem statement, but your first draft should come from your own thinking.",
